lisa-design:
Fully-compliant controls now expose their own compliance evidence as leaf children (control -> evidence, relationship=has-evidence), alongside implementing/documenting controls and risks. "Fully compliant" = the control's own status (from its filters' latest evidence) is satisfied AND it has >=1 matching stream. Evidence shown = the latest stream per matching stream (deduped), NOT shown for non-satisfied controls. Implemented by refactoring evidence loading: new relational.LoadLatestEvidenceStreams(db, componentID) returns []LatestEvidenceStream{UUID,Title,State,Reason,Collected(end),Expires,Labels} via the loose-index-scan CTE; the engine loads streams once, evaluates each filter's scope in Go, and stores per-control matched stream indices (evidenceStreamsByControl) + derives controlStatus from those streams (statusFromStreams). GetEvidenceStatusCountsByFilters was reimplemented on top of LoadLatestEvidenceStreams (kept as a public helper; no longer used by the engine). controlFullyCompliant() gates both the childrenCount bump and the evidence children. Perf unchanged (~0.5s /children on live data — streams loaded once). Risk-linked evidence (risk_evidence_links) and control compliance evidence (filters) are distinct sources but share evidence:<streamUuid> keys so the graph dedups.
